  "notes": "A shared context (the map period), two loaders, each a dataset dragged from the Data Catalog, and a Harmonize node that saves the riverside tracts as a computed dataset (curio_save_file), which the depth nodes read with curio_computed_path, feed two scenarios. Each runs the package's Flood Projection for the map period, then an Autark map of the depth with the tracts' borders over it; one Autark map shows the tracts' vulnerability for both. A Python node takes the absolute change in depth (curio_raster_calculate) for an Autark map; one Flood Projection node runs every compared period for both scenarios for a bar chart, and the scatter reads the tract depths stacked (the dataset inputs) and names each circle's scenario from __input__."
